gn-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts — stored publication and approved-story cleanup","src/daemon/design-review-rpc.ts — coordinator, admission and publication wiring","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts — historical source and permanent-report requalification","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts — recovery, publication reservation and cleanup fencing","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress-view.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/completion.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/cleanup.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts — explicit recovery and publication retry","src/workflow/review/design-review/checkpoint.ts — immutable history and atomic persistence","src/workflow/review/design-review/publication.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/read.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/approval.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/cleanup.ts","src/workflow/gates.ts — approval and repeated cleanup paths","src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts — fenced design approval and cleanup","src/daemon/threads/review-state-contract.ts","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts — workerScript and reclamation contract","src/daemon/threads/__tests__/review-state-concurrency.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/recovery.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/cleanup.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/recovery.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/publication.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/cleanup.test.ts","src/mcp/code-review/schema.ts","src/mcp/design-review/schema.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts — review metadata contract","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt — review DTO lookup","package.json — build pipeline","tsconfig.json — compiled worker inclusion"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the preservation tests explicitly cover failed admission followed by a successful next attempt, permanent publication, approval cleanup and post-cleanup history reads for both families. Assert that technical diagnostics survive without becoming review findings or changing prior approval evidence.","Add an explicit zero-provider-call assertion for publication retries through real worker routing, including lost publication receipts and retries after worker exit; the existing family tests already establish useful model-free baselines."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected all assigned definitions, adherence declarations and generated HTML companions. Sequence and component content preserve the intended authority boundaries and durable acknowledgment order. The ER companion contradicts lifecycle cardinalities. Actual rendering verification was blocked.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/erDefinition; S001/er-model.html embedded erDiagram","message":"The generated ER diagram requires every ReviewIdentity to have exactly one ReviewWorker and one ControllerOwner. Durable identities must survive worker exit, and daemon-reviewed identities have no controller owner. It also renders attempts as zero-or-more despite the authored minimum_cardinality of one. Correct the inverse ownership cardinalities and regenerate: each durable identity has zero-or-one active worker, zero-or-one controller owner and one-or-more persisted attempts.","evidenceReferences":["/body/erDefinition/classes/ReviewIdentity/attributes/attempts/minimum_cardinality","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html: ReviewWorker ||--|| ReviewIdentity","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html: ControllerOwner ||--o{ ReviewIdentity","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html: ReviewIdentity ||--o