ence.","Add an explicit zero-provider-call assertion for publication retries through real worker routing, including lost publication receipts and retries after worker exit; the existing family tests already establish useful model-free baselines."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected all assigned definitions, adherence declarations and generated HTML companions. Sequence and component content preserve the intended authority boundaries and durable acknowledgment order. The ER companion contradicts lifecycle cardinalities. Actual rendering verification was blocked.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/erDefinition; S001/er-model.html embedded erDiagram","message":"The generated ER diagram requires every ReviewIdentity to have exactly one ReviewWorker and one ControllerOwner. Durable identities must survive worker exit, and daemon-reviewed identities have no controller owner. It also renders attempts as zero-or-more despite the authored minimum_cardinality of one. Correct the inverse ownership cardinalities and regenerate: each durable identity has zero-or-one active worker, zero-or-one controller owner and one-or-more persisted attempts.","evidenceReferences":["/body/erDefinition/classes/ReviewIdentity/attributes/attempts/minimum_cardinality","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html: ReviewWorker ||--|| ReviewIdentity","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html: ControllerOwner ||--o{ ReviewIdentity","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html: ReviewIdentity ||--o{ CheckpointAttempt","LLD.md sections 3.1, 3.4–3.6: durable history, optional controller ownership and worker reclamation","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts:115–120"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/erDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/componentDependencyDefinition","/body/adherence","/body/companions","document:line:175","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/sequence-diagram.html","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/component-dependency.html","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/review-worker-isolation-lld-20261109.json","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts","src/daemon/threads/review-state-contract.ts"],"limitations":["Actual renderings of er-model.html, sequence-diagram.html and component-dependency.html could not be inspected: the in-app browser was unavailable and Chrome rejected local file URLs under its security policy. Embedded Mermaid sources, descriptions, tables and rendering setup were inspected; diagram rendering success and visual legibility remain unverified."],"advice":["The admission-state prose and client contract tests adequately describe the changed pending/failure behavior for this assignment; no additional UX mock is necessary without a proposed layout or interaction change."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"All inventory units have substantive coverage in the five completed chunks. The current canonical artifact and live document match the reviewed baseline. Scope, acknowledgment ordering, immutable admission inputs, trusted ownership, explicit recovery, publication, approval exclusions and migration a