 ArtifactReviewViewDto and parsing","vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts — review rendering contract lookup","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/review/ArtifactContentPane.kt — review rendering contract lookup"],"limitations":["Actual renderings of docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html and docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/sequence-diagram.html were not verified. The in-app browser was unavailable, and Chrome's browser security policy rejected the local file URL. Generated Mermaid source was inspected; this does not establish visual correctness."],"advice":["Make the proposed progress wire contract more concrete by naming the design admission phase and specifying how unknown task/chunk totals and admission diagnostics appear. Current code progress requires numeric totalTasks, design progress requires numeric totalChunks, and the live IDE artifact views currently carry review metadata rather than an explicit admission-progress DTO."]},{"chunkId":"evidence","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned sections align with the originating ISSUE. Recovery preserves accepted feedback, publication retries remain model-free, approval excludes unverified admission, and cleanup requires scope fencing and permanent evidence preservation. Migration covers coordinated restart, compiled-worker packaging, historical compatibility and reader-compatible rollback. No blocking defect was demonstrated in this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-desi