63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/sequence-diagram.html","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/component-dependency.html","/tmp/review-worker-sequence.png","/tmp/review-worker-components.png","/tmp/review-worker-diagram-render-evidence.txt","src/shared/process-group.ts:65","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:40","src/native/process-broker/README.md","Checkpoint attempt 2: inventory, plan coverage and accepted scope/runtime/admission/evidence/visuals results","Checkpoint attempt 1: report and all four effective finding origins"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Runtime chunk finding runtime-003 remains blocking: full-daemon crash recovery needs durable fence reconstruction, an explicit clearance protocol and a daemon-crash regression. It is not duplicated here.","Retain the admission chunk's optional clarification of admission.validation and the runtime chunk's resolveBin subprocess-inventory advice.","The previous rendering limitations are satisfied by current fresh visual inspection. Implementation tests remain future validation, not a missing LLD review check."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-001"},"rationale":"The original individual-worker crash defect is addressed by main-owned process leases created before spawning, host cancellation and output ownership, confirmed disposal requirements, replacement fencing and registration-race tests. Full-daemon loss is separately covered by current runtime-003 and remains unresolved.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md section 3.6: main-owned native command leases, synchronous lease-before-spawn registration and confirmed disposal","LLD.md section 6: worker crashes before command request, during registration and after child start","Checkpoint attempt 2 completedChunks/runtime: fresh runtime assessment and runtime-003","src/shared/process-group.ts:108"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime","evidence","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"runtime","findingId":"runtime-002"},"rationale":"The design now explicitly adds a parent-owned 30-second deadline covering both readiness and durable admission save, rejects late acknowledgments, returns promptly, and retains targeted fencing during reclamation. Real-worker fixtures cover missing readiness and a blocked save.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md section 3.3: parent-owned bootstrap deadline and late-save handling","LLD.md section 5: worker boot and admission-storage error response","LLD.md section 6: never-ready and pre-save-hang fixtures","Checkpoint attempt 2 completedChunks/runtime and completedChunks/admission"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["runtime","admission","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"admission","findingId":"admission-001"},"rationale":"The contradictory ER definition and companion declaration were removed. The authoritative relationship table now specifies zero-or-one active worker, zero-or-one controller owner and one-or-more persisted attempts for each durable review identity.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md section 3.1: authoritative ownership/cardinality table","Canonical /body/companions and /body/adherence: current sequence/component artifacts only","Checkpoint attempt 2 completedChunks/admission and completedChunks/visuals"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["admission","visuals","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-001"},"rationale":"The same ER cardinality contradiction is corrected through the authoritative prose table and removal of the obsolete ER artifact from current declarations. Both remaining companions match their definitions and were visually inspected using current PNG renderings.","evi