ive-process helpers, and component diagram source/rendering. The revised durable-intent and recovery protocol addresses daemon-loss discovery and ordering, but its required human clearance authority is unsupported by the broker contract it proposes to reuse.","findings":[{"id":"runtime-004","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/3 and /body/dataModelChanges/5; LLD.md:129,167","message":"Specify the approval-broker extension needed to enforce operator-only resource clearance. The design requires trusted operator identity and rejects controller automation, but the existing approval.answer handler discards trusted connection context, the broker accepts the first matching requestId/decision from any caller, and ApprovalAnswer contains no responder identity or human-required provenance. Merely asking this broker directly can bypass commonApproval auto-allow, but cannot establish the stronger operator attestation promised here. An automated subscriber can answer the pending clearance request and produce the same approval outcome as the human UI. Define the trusted answering-channel eligibility, context propagation, exact-review/guard receipt binding and broker/client contract changes, with tests proving an ordinary controller or automated answer cannot release the fence.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md:129","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md:167","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts:1591 — approval.answer forwards only params","src/daemon/approval.ts:32 — answer accepts requestId/decision without trusted caller context","src/daemon/approval-broker.ts:72 — answer validates pending identity and expiry, without responder authority","src/daemon/tools/types.ts:58 — ApprovalAnswer contains only requestId and decision","src/shared/types.ts:1069 — approval request/answer contracts lack operator eligibility or human-required provenance","vscode-plugin/sr